        "original_id": "b96d9bd6-886d-54d5-82f7-8f09cf53f1a8",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Mary Jane Phillips-Matz, Auguste Mariette, Temistocle Solera, Antonio Ghislanzoni, Giuseppe Verdi\n- Organizations: Columbia University, Smith College\n- Places: Lebanon, Ohio, Italy, United States, Busseto, Upper Manhattan, New York City\n- Works: Aida\n- Topics: Verdi research, opera authorship, higher education\n\nFacts:\n- Columbia University was established in 1754 as a private Ivy League research university in Upper Manhattan, New York City.\n- Mary Jane Phillips-Matz was born in Lebanon, Ohio and was educated at Smith College and Columbia University.\n- Mary Jane Phillips-Matz lived for many years in Italy.\n- After returning to the United States in the early 1970s, Mary Jane Phillips-Matz spent her summers in Busseto, Giuseppe Verdi's hometown, and continued her exhaustive research into his life.\n- In discussing Aida, Antonio Ghislanzoni's scheme follows a scenario often attributed to the French Egyptologist Auguste Mariette.\n- Mary Jane Phillips-Matz argued that the actual source for the Aida scenario was Temistocle Solera.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
